pe":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/felipecarrillo100/cloudfrontize/commits/97e9e1110a664d95c8d5baf31d3e9ef55c40f89e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T15:01:48Z","email":"felipe.carrillo.romero@hexagon.com","name":"felipe.carrillo.romero"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T15:01:48Z","email":"felipe.carrillo.romero@hexagon.com","name":"felipe.carrillo.romero"},"message":"fix(edge): return 503 on strict-mode Lambda@Edge timeouts; add CI typecheck\n\nIn --strict mode a timed-out Lambda@Edge hook returned { _timeout: true },\nwhich the Orchestrator never checked, so the request continued to the\norigin as if the hook had succeeded. Timeouts now produce a 503\nLambdaLimitExceeded response, matching CloudFront, and a timeout in a\nresponse hook stops the remaining hooks from running.\n\nTypechecking:\n- tsconfig: switch to module \"preserve\" / moduleResolution \"bundler\"\n  (node10 resolution is a hard error in TypeScript 6) and drop ui-src,\n  which has its own config\n- add tsconfig.typecheck.json (src + bin) and an `npm run typecheck`\n  script; prepublishOnly now runs it before building\n- add a CI workflow that runs the typecheck on PRs and pushes to main\n- fix the type errors it surfaced: missing exposedHeaders on EdgeRunner\n  early returns, and the ''success'' telemetry event type\n\nTests:\n- multi_origin: point the S3 endpoint at a reserved, closed port rather\n  than assuming localhost:9999 is unused\n- zzz_ui_api: serve stub UI assets via a new uiDir option so the suite\n  no longer needs a Vite build; make the static-asset tests async so\n  failures don''t hang until the 30s timeout\n- timeout_fidelity: add end-to-end tests for strict viewer-request and\n  viewer-response timeouts returning 503","tree":{"sha":"4b4eeff9d219d85dc0d099261eb9507395dec966","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/felipecarrillo100/cloudfrontize/git/trees/4b4eeff9d219d85dc0d099261eb9507395dec966"},"url":"https://api.github.com/re