e5159e94d6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Nicolasgh91/portfolio/commits/a6d19c810c4a1ce20dd4936974c2e6e5159e94d6"}],"sha":"ec84f51e32e39f236b6ee4011ba456c8f0936abb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Nicolasgh91/portfolio/commits/ec84f51e32e39f236b6ee4011ba456c8f0936abb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/100943553?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nicolasgh91/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nicolasgh91/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nicolasgh91/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nicolasgh91/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Nicolasgh91","id":100943553,"login":"Nicolasgh91","node_id":"U_kgDOBgRGwQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nicolasgh91/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nicolasgh91/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nicolasgh91/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nicolasgh91/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nicolasgh91/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nicolasgh91","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Nicolasgh91/portfolio/commits/a6d19c810c4a1ce20dd4936974c2e6e5159e94d6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-29T12:43:02Z","email":"100943553+Nicolasgh91@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nicolás Gabriel Hruszczak"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-29T12:43:02Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Claude/codebase audit zne pt (#34)\n\n* refactor: codebase audit phase 1 + 2 cleanup\n\nRemoves dead code, replaces hardcoded colors with tokens, consolidates\nthe duplicated FAQ component, extracts inline scripts and empty-state\nmarkup, and centralizes Footer collection loading.\n\nPhase 1 (safe deletions + token discipline):\n- Delete unused ProjectDemo.astro, LogoMarquee.astro, hero_templates.webp v1.\n- Document /schemas/ intent (backend-only, preserved for future consumer).\n- Replace literal hex (#fbbf24, #f59e0b, #475569, #94a3b8, #f1f5f9, #ffffff,\n  #34d399, #1d9e75, #eab308) with token vars across BlogCard, ProjectCard,\n  ContactForm, HeroSection.\n- Add --ease-out-expo and --ease-out-overshoot tokens; refactor CapabilityCard\n  and BlogCard to consume them.\n- Hoist a single posts query in blog/[slug].astro getStaticPaths and pass\n  related posts via props (drops one redundant getCollection call per page).\n\nPhase 2 (component consolidation):\n- Merge FAQAccordion into FaqSection via variant: \"default\" | \"darkBand\";\n  delete FAQAccordion.astro and update servicios.astro consumer.\n- Extract Footer collection loading into src/lib/footer-data.ts so the\n  component stays presentational and ordering rules live in one place.\n- Move chat widget bootstrap from inline <script> in Layout.astro to\n  /public/scripts/chat-widget.js (smaller HTML on every page; CSP-friendly).\n- Extract Nav.astro 140-line client controller into\n  src/components/scripts/nav-controller.ts (Nav.astro becomes markup-focused).\n- Add reusable EmptyState.astro and adopt in blog/index.astro and\n  plantillas.astro.\n\nVerified: npm test (33/33 pass), npm run check (0 errors), npm run build\n(98 pages built), npm run lint (clean).\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01TCtkJ7J22Sg1twyd5vrm1b\n\n* refactor: codebase audit phase 3 — page decomposition + lint guard\n\nSplits the four largest pages (talento, plantillas, servicios,\nblog/[slug]) into thinner page templates plus focused lib/data modules,\nand adds a script that fails the lint pipeline if a raw hex literal\nslips outside src/styles/tokens.css.\n\nPage line counts (before → after):\n- src/pages/blog/[slug].astro:  543 → 479\n- src/pages/servicios.astro:    535 → 450\n- src/pages/plantillas.astro:   706 → 641\n- src/pages/talento.astro:      734 → 654\n                              ----   ----\n                              2518   2224  (−294)\n\nExtractions:\n- src/lib/blog-cover.ts: COVER_BY_KEY map and resolveCover() (cover image\n  optimization + OG dimensions for blog posts).\n- src/lib/blog-jsonld.ts: buildArticleJsonLd, buildBlogBreadcrumbJsonLd.\n- src/lib/service-pricing.ts: parsePriceFromFrontmatter,\n  resolveServicePrice, serviceCardPayload, PRICE_INQUIRE.\n- src/lib/services-jsonld.ts: buildServicesJsonLd (catalog @graph).\n- src/lib/templates-jsonld.ts: buildTemplatesCatalogJsonLd,\n  buildPricingPlansJsonLd.\n- src/data/templates-faq.ts: catalog FAQ entries (was inline ~50 lines).\n- src/data/talent-skills.ts: capabilities + softSkills static lists +\n  projectStatusLabel.\n- FaqItem moves to src/lib/faq-taxonomy.ts (re-exported from\n  FaqSection.astro for backwards compatibility) so plain TS modules can\n  reference it without an Astro file dependency.\n\nLint guard:\n- scripts/check-no-raw-hex.mjs walks src/, flags raw #hex literals\n  outside tokens.css unless an `allow-raw-hex: <reason>` marker appears\n  on the line or up to 8 lines above.\n- Wired into `npm run lint` via `lint:no-raw-hex`.\n- Three legitimate exceptions documented inline:\n  - Layout.astro <meta name=\"theme-color\">  (attribute can''t take CSS vars).\n  - HeroSection.astro macOS traffic-light dots (decorative brand colors).\n  - BlogCard.astro SVG stroke + ContactForm.astro snackbar text (literal\n    contrast values over a fixed-color surface).\n\nVerified: npm test (33/33), npm run check (0 errors), npm run build\n(98 pages), npm run lint (clean, including no-raw-hex).\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01TCtkJ7J22Sg1twyd5vrm1b\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0c443c7b91adfc8f36519b64e93f2b520727d47b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Nicolasgh91/portfolio/git/trees/0c443c7b91adfc8f36519b64e93f2b520727d47b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Nicolasgh91/portfolio/git/commits/a6d19c810c4a1ce20dd4936