subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Nicolasgh91/portfolio/commits/53d10fad4f386d1e75f4e3de262b1d3306e915fd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-13T12:10:40Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-13T12:10:40Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"fix(csp): emit Astro bundled scripts as external files\n\nCSP `script-src ''self''` (set in vercel.json by the M-05 hardening) blocked\nsmall Astro-bundled scripts that Vite was inlining as\n`<script type=\"module\">...</script>` (default `assetsInlineLimit` ~4 KB),\nplus every `<script define:vars>` block (always inline by contract).\n\nThis regressed three features on the Vercel preview:\n- BackToTop button never showed (visibility script blocked).\n- Chat widget never appeared (iframe creator script blocked).\n- SlideViewer arrows / fullscreen unresponsive; only the first slide visible.\n\nTwo-part fix:\n- astro.config.mjs: set `vite.build.assetsInlineLimit: 0` so all bundled\n  scripts emit as external `/_astro/*.js` files (CSP `''self''`-allowed).\n- Drop `define:vars` / `is:inline` from per-instance scripts and switch\n  to `document.querySelectorAll(''[data-*]'').forEach(...)` initialization:\n  - SlideViewer.astro (uses existing `data-slide-viewer`).\n  - blog/TableOfContents.astro (uses existing `data-toc-root`).\n  - blog/ShareBar.astro (adds `data-share-bar`).\n  - FaqSection.astro (adds `data-faq-animated-root`).\n  - pages/plantillas.astro (drops `is:inline`; bundled external).\n\nVerification: `npm run build` produces zero inline `<script type=\"module\">`\nbodies anywhere in `dist/`. Typecheck and the 26-test suite remain green.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01N7zygd3Fu3aurqSoidFuZF","tree":{"sha":"7f0cb03f75ff025c5d8df749fa65bdcc4550d064","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Nicolasgh91/portfolio/git/trees/7f0cb03f75ff025c5d8df749fa65bdcc4550d064"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Nicolasgh91/portfolio/git/commits/53d10fad4f386d1e75f4e3de262b1d3306e915fd","verification":{"payload":"tree 7f0cb03f75ff025c5d8df749fa65bdcc4550d064\nparent 7a1903a2388d87a52bcf62cbd7fcfccbc04688e6\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1776082240 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1776082240 +0000\n\nfix(csp): emit Astro bundled scripts as external files\n\nCSP `script-src ''self''` (set in vercel.json by the M-05 hardening) blocked\nsmall Astro-bundled scripts that Vite was inlining as\n`<script type=\"module\">...</script>` (default `assetsInlineLimit` ~4 KB),\nplus every `<script define:vars>` block (always inline by contract).\n\nThis regressed three features on the Vercel preview:\n- BackToTop button never showed (visibility script blocked).\n- Chat widget never appeared (iframe creator script blocked).\n- SlideViewer arrows / fullscreen unresponsive; only the first slide visible.\n\nTwo-part fix:\n- astro.config.mjs: set `vite.build.assetsInlineLimit: 0` so all bundled\n  scripts emit as external `/_astro/*.js` files (CSP `''self''`-allowed).\n- Drop `define:vars` / `is:inline` from per-instance scripts and switch\n  to `document.querySelectorAll(''[data-*]'').forEach(...)` initialization:\n  - SlideViewer.astro (uses existing `data-slide-viewer`).\n  - blog/TableOfContents.astro (uses existing `data-toc-root`).\n  - blog/ShareBar.astro (adds `data-share-bar`).\n  - FaqSection.astro (adds `data-faq-animated-root`).\n  - pages/plantillas.astro (drops `is:inline`; bundled external).\n\nVerification: `npm run build` produces zero inline `<script type=\"module\">`\nbodies anywhere in `dist/`. Typecheck and the 26-test suite remain green.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01N7zygd3Fu3aurqSoidFuZF\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz2